WEBVTT

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:14.650
<i>Sometimes, we rely on our contrary hearts</i>

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:14.650
<i>Toki ni urahara na kokoro o tayori ni</i>

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.750
<i>Tattoo Kiss, the last resort is a
mission which changes the future</i>

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.750
<i>Tattoo Kiss kirifuda wa mirai o kaeru Mission</i>

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:21.420
<i>Tattoo Kiss, the last resort is a
mission which changes the future</i>

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:21.420
<i>Tattoo Kiss kirifuda wa mirai o kaeru Mission</i>

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:21.420
New Wings

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:29.360
<i>There is no place for ambiguous answers in love</i>

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:29.360
<i>Koi ni aimai na kotae wa iranai</i>

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:36.840
<i>Even while pretending not to see the
impossible reality, we bet</i>

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:36.840
<i>Arienai genjitsu minai furi shite mo Bet</i>

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:43.110
<i>Hard to obtain truth. Can you feel me now?</i>

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:43.110
<i>Egatai shinjitsu Can U feel me now?</i>

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.650
<i>Say what to myself who gets excited easily?</i>

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.650
<i>Nesshiyasui jibun ni Say What?</i>

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.020
<i>I'm confused, what to say</i>

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.020
<i>Tomadou iibun</i>

00:00:52.620 --> 00:01:00.230
<i>Dreamin' the never-waking dream,
the falling fate</i>

00:00:52.620 --> 00:01:00.230
<i>Dreamin' samenai yume ochiteku sadame</i>

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:06.000
<i>Don't stop lovin' can't stop lovin' you
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:06.000
<i>Don't stop lovin' Can't stop lovin' U
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:15.340
<i>I believe in you even if I lose everything for it</i>

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:15.340
<i>Believe in U hikikae ni subete ushinatte mo</i>

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.870
<i>Still lovin' can't stop lovin' you
No no no</i>

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.870
<i>Still lovin' can't stop loving' U
No no no</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:27.490
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:27.490
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.130
When that happens, what you have to do
is take your challengers head-on

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:39.170
and become a wall for them to overcome.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.070
And when the time comes,

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:44.130
you must fight with all your strength
and be defeated.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:48.810
Giving your challengers a battle will be
another important duty of yours from now on.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.050
Don't forget that.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.480
All right.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.250
Miss Layla is right.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:02:00.820
Really even I think that there's no such thing
as a world without battles.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.390
But even now I still sort of think it would be nice

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.380
if there weren't any battles on the stage at least.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:13.600
Challengers, adventurers, pioneers...

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.560
All who are called by such names are fools.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:22.240
What awaits the fools who pursue
the dreams no one else dreams

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.150
is either scorn... or applause.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.350
Be my dream, Sora.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:37.190
To the Amazing Promised Place

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:37.190
"To the Amazing Promised Place"

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.990
To the Amazing Promised Place

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.530
Okay Mom, Dad, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.370
Yep.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.270
I'm looking forward to it.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:52.940
Ken, are you sure it wasn't a burden on your
parents to take in my whole family?

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.580
Well, my mom's the one that offered,
so it's probably okay.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.580
Then I guess it's all right...

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:00.980
So tomorrow's the opening day at last, huh?

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.220
Although it looks like they still haven't
finished construction...

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.290
Yeah. It is a pretty big construction
project, after all.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.620
No big deal, we're almost there.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.130
Right. I'm sorry.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.460
You shouldn't apologize too lightly.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.730
You gave us a job really worth doing.
I'm actually grateful.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.030
We'll make this brilliant.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.930
I'm counting on you!

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.500
Did May and Rosetta's maneuver
end up getting okayed?

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:33.820
The directorial team was supposed to
decide at yesterday's rehearsal,

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:36.980
but Miss Cathy tested them again today.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.750
I guess I'll okay it,

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:44.190
but Rosetta, I'd like a more
commanding presence from you.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.180
You can do that, right?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.920
Of course I can.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.230
Oh, good.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.670
And Anna's clown team too?

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.700
Yep.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.500
So...

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.810
We get to do it?

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.180
Yay!

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.180
Hey... I can't breathe... seriously...

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.710
That special training was really worth it, huh?!

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.710
Hey... I can't breathe... seriously...

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:02.140
Hey... I can't breathe... seriously...

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.200
Everybody got their dreams, huh?

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.180
But aren't you going to perform anymore, Ken?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.320
Me?

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.660
Yeah. I mean, really you wanted
to be a performer, right?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.830
So when you found a path
as a clown in Anna's team,

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:21.490
I thought "Hooray! Congratulations!" but...

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.940
That's not my dream now.
That's a dream from a long time ago.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.800
It is?

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.510
Oh, that's right! I hear our
opening show is sold out.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:33.940
Really?!

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.780
Yep.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.010
I was concerned since curtain
is at an unusual time,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.000
but now we have one less thing to worry about.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:43.720
Yuri was the one who planned
the tie-in with the tour company.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:48.490
Well, well. So he has his father's
sound business sense?

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.020
It looks like he'll make a good partner for you.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.360
Maybe I'll make my confession...

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.370
Confession?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:58.530
I...

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.400
Yes?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.470
I'm full of myself.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:02.940
Huh? What? What's this about?

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.630
Please explain.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:08.810
I thought you were helping me out so much

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:11.750
because you were entrusting
your own dream to me.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:12.910
Huh?

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.580
Oh, don't get me wrong,

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.420
I do understand it's really because I'm
the one most hopelessly in need of help!

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.220
I do get it, really!

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:23.260
But every time I look at it that way, it makes me
feel like "Okay, I'll give this my best!"

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.660
and it gives me strength,

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.900
so I've been letting myself think that way.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:31.330
Ken, it's thanks to you that
I've been able to come this far.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.320
Thank you.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.540
You're not full of yourself.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:36.470
Huh?

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:37.510
But from now on,

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:42.180
you'll become someone who shoulders
lots of people's dreams, not just mine.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.240
Yeah.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:46.580
So, shall we go? After all,
we have to get to bed early tonight.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.050
Yep!

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.720
A stage with no battles, eh?

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:56.190
It's definitely a ridiculous dream,

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.990
but I'm at the age where I want to try
believing in those foolish dreams.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:02.530
The only people who can become true stars

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.830
are the ones who, as they come to realize
their dream is foolish,

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.500
believe in it even more and keep pursuing it.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.030
That's a very difficult thing...

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.010
That day,

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.440
everybody called up their own memories

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.640
as if they were being led
by Sora's performance.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:21.770
The memories of when they wanted everybody
to smile, both themselves and others.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:27.990
That's a true Kaleido Star's maneuver,
one Sora arrived at on her own power.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.860
I'm sure all the audience's hearts
will become one.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:31.990
Don't you think that's right?

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.660
What I don't think is right

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.660
is that you were practicing the Angel's Maneuver
without even telling ME.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.840
I'm sorry.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:45.170
When the apology comes so meekly
it sort of throws me off...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.710
You want to take my car tomorrow?

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.280
I'm not going tomorrow.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.040
What? Why not?

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:56.280
I already know Sora's going to
become a true Kaleido Star,

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.380
and I'm not sure it's good for me, who lost,
to go looking like I'm her guardian.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.790
Even if you did lose the competition,

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:08.330
I think to Sora you'll always be the
Layla Hamilton she admires.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.370
Why not go watch her?

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.460
Okay.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.120
That was fast!

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.970
I mean, why are you so meek today?

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:18.540
Because your advice is sound.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.710
I see, I didn't know you thought of me
that way. I'm flattered.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.210
In that case, be that meek after
we get back to Broadway too.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.340
That I can't promise you.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.590
I thought not...

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:34.020
Anyway, I think you should watch
the show tomorrow.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.880
I have a feeling something else
is going to happen.

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:39.890
Something?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.990
Yep. Something.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.830
Angel's Maneuver jump!

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.500
Jump!

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:50.570
Oh, Sora.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.540
Welcome back, Sora!

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.410
I'm back Marion, Jonathan!

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:00.240
Everybody's still doing their individual practice,
so there's nobody in the dorm.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.450
Okay! Then I'll go at it too and...

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.020
Sora.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.020
Okay! Then I'll go at it too and...

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:04.450
Sora.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:05.590
Yes?

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.290
You're going to rest.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:08.990
Oh, but...

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:11.160
Everybody's seen you trying your best,

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.660
so they're doing their best to catch up to you as
much as they can, even if it's just a little.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:18.000
So you can take a rest, and believe in everyone.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.500
Okay.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.570
Sora, I've decided.

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:26.370
I'm going to take a real audition
and join the Kaleido Stage!

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:27.810
Really?!

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.550
Jonathan says he'll try too,
since he's got nothing to lose.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:34.570
Amazing!

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.480
Wait, why do you understand him?!

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:39.680
Okay, do your best tomorrow!

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.590
B-Bye-bye!

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.590
Take care...

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.430
Well, I'll be going now too.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.260
Okay, thanks.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.940
A stage without battles, eh?

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:05.550
I heard you always personally inspect
the trapezes you'll use.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:07.250
I guess it's true.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:08.880
What do you want?

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:13.150
I thought maybe we could talk, as two people
who couldn't completely become demons.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.620
It's true,

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.890
perhaps I just couldn't leave Sora alone

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:19.230
when I saw she couldn't completely break
herself apart on her own.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:23.800
On a basic level, the Angel's Maneuver
is something that can be performed alone.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:26.200
We're just extra.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.740
Just extra, eh?

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:29.740
Those women are strong.

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:32.040
They can run anywhere, all by themselves.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:36.580
But sometimes they want to
lean on somebody, just a little.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:39.050
We just need to support them
during those times, that's all.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.320
That's our role.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.150
Just like angels, huh?

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.390
Yep.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:48.050
So I guess it would make sense that
we couldn't make it as demons.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:51.230
Manami, Sayaka, and Miki say they'll come too.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:52.290
I see.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:55.060
I wonder if Yume will really watch.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.000
It looks like you can't sleep.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.400
Nope.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:02.600
Well, tomorrow I'll just believe in myself
and give it all I've got.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.770
Goodnight, Fool.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.140
Goodnight.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:28.100
The Angel's Maneuver, eh?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.200
I hear it's also called "The Fool's Maneuver."

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:36.600
It says Odette fights with the part of her own
heart that starts to doubt the prince's love.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.170
So basically it's about how you have a
tough time when you date a popular guy?

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:46.340
Odette keeps on believing that there's
an angel heart inside Odile too.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.680
That sounds like Sora.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.950
Pretty nice, isn't it Yume?

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.150
She's in a good mood.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:55.260
We could've done the afternoon showing.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:56.490
I'm fine.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.090
Ack, I can't read this!

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.220
Is it going to start soon?

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.530
It's like, a full house, even though
it's so early in the morning.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:09.230
They say there's supposed to be a stage event
cool enough to warrant an early-morning show.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.210
I wanted to see your Odette as well, Miss.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:15.470
I'll never stand on this stage again.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:18.740
Did you invite anyone, Mr. Leon?

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.980
I sent Alain passes to the show
and plane tickets,

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.720
but he might have sold them to buy alcohol.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:26.790
No, he wouldn't do that... I don't think...

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:33.460
I know your old partners will come too,
and get their smiles back.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:37.060
Do you still believe in a stage without battles?

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.500
I've decided to believe in it.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:43.770
The Legendary Great Maneuver is something
you can't do unless you believe in it absolutely.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:46.110
So I'm sure the Angel's Maneuver
is the same way.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.840
By the way, I'm sorry about that.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.880
Huh? About what?

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:55.720
When I said Layla was a lukewarm performer,
you told me to apologize, didn't you?

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.520
Ah...

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:03.490
I thought she'd retired after pulling off
the Legendary Great Maneuver with you

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:05.480
so she could keep that glory forever.

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:12.870
But Layla mastered the Angel's Maneuver
and came back, fully prepared to lose,

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.400
for your sake.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.130
For my sake...

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.770
If you hadn't fought Layla that day,

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:24.210
your confidence most likely
wouldn't be as firm as it is now.

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:27.440
You're right.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.290
Please raise the curtain.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:48.270
Let's all get the very best applause together!

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:54.000
Next is Scene 5.
Odette is going to meet the prince.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:59.010
The prince falls in love...

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:00.910
He's got a nice expression on his face!

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.270
The material is good, after all.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:07.640
Scene 11: The ball.
Anna's clown team is on.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.490
Wow. Anna's looking good!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:20.590
It's time at last for her special
training to be put to the test!

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.290
Don't go!

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.300
They like it...

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:33.300
There's nothing there, but it looks like
she's being pulled by a string!

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:36.240
Come back!

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.180
This laughter is for me!

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:46.220
I finally got it, Papa, Mama...

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:48.650
Congratulations, Anna.

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:53.590
Next it's Demon Lake.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:58.660
The prince has his heart stolen by Odile!

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:01.600
Odile is the demon heart.

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:04.570
Mysterious and bold,

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.670
more lively than Odette!

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:10.140
Yay!

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.200
Big sister, you look so cool!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:15.640
Change the backdrop to the deep forest.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:25.880
Odile leads the prince into the deep forest
and is trapped there as well.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:31.290
And Odette discovers the conflict
in Odile's heart.

